On-core Ed25519 + secp256k1 verify on the RTL SoC (#4, W1), 2026-10-20
Branch 4-ed25519-soc (based on integrate-prs @ 48f4c13, the #33-#50 stack).
Top: muserisc_soc_top (in-house core + L1 I$/D$ + fabric + boot ROM +
CLINT + PLIC + 16550 UART + crypto AXI-Lite bridge @0x2000_0000),
external RAM modelled by tb/cpp/soc_rtl_tb.cpp.
Host: Apple M3 (arm64, macOS), Homebrew Verilator 5.044,
riscv64-elf-gcc 16.2.0 (-march=rv64imafdc -O1, as sim/Makefile).

Firmware (sw/soc-tests/, shared driver soc_crypto_drv.h):
- crypto_soc_test.c: SHA-256 (accelerator), secp256k1 field mul KAT,
  Jacobian 2*G, ECDSA verify of the sw/ec_ops.py frozen vector, and
  NEW stage 5: the same verify with z bit 0 flipped must reject (the
  file header claimed this check but main() never ran it).
- ed25519_soc_test.c (NEW): Ed25519 verify of RFC 8032 sec. 7.1 TEST 1
  and TEST 2 (the vectors in sw/ec_ops.py). Every Curve25519 field
  add/sub/mul runs on the accelerator with MODSEL=1 (p = 2^255-19).
  Hash step: SHA-512 is computed IN SOFTWARE ON THE CORE (FIPS 180-4
  code in the firmware, checked against the SHA-512("abc") KAT in
  stage 1); k = SHA-512(R||A||M) mod L in software. No precomputed
  digests. Verify = cofactorless RFC 8032 5.1.7 / ref10 form:
  decode A, check encode([S]B + [k](-A)) == R; extended Edwards
  coordinates, one joint double-and-add ladder.
  Stages: 1 SHA-512 KAT; 2 field KATs sqrt(-1)^2 = -1 and
  d*121666 = -121665; 3 TEST 1 accept; 4 TEST 2 accept; 5 TEST 2
  with S bit 0 flipped rejects at the point compare (full verify
  math runs); 6 TEST 2 with S+L (non-canonical) rejects.
Reference code: variable-time, NOT constant-time (W2/W4).

